(A3 — reading a line from a file into a global buffer inside a function must
 not be silently skipped; the new pointer and line contents must be visible
 afterwards.)

open a file for writing called f at "./test_304_input.txt".
Write "first line" to f.
Close f.

open a file for reading called src at "./test_304_input.txt".
a buffer called buf is "".
Resize buf to 4 bytes.

To 'readit'.
  Read line from src into buf.


To 'check'.
  If buf's length is greater than 0, print "read ok".
  Print buf.


'readit'.
'check'.

Close src.
Delete the file "./test_304_input.txt".
